WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.711
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:17.004
Unit nineteen: Speaking Part 2: The Long Turn. Today you will speak for one to two minutes on a topic using a clear structure.

4
00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:19.875
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:24.008
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.909
Cue card.

7
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:29.799
Cue card means a card with the topic and prompts.

8
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:31.988
Read the cue card carefully.

9
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:35.073
Your turn. Say: Cue card.

10
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:39.039
Cue card.

11
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.005
Preparation time.

12
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:44.968
Preparation time means one minute to plan your talk.

13
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.351
Use the preparation time.

14
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.194
Your turn. Say: Preparation time.

15
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.441
Preparation time.

16
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.359
Long turn.

17
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.756
Long turn means your one to two minute talk.

18
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.083
The long turn is Part 2.

19
00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:06.510
Your turn. Say: Long turn.

20
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.774
Long turn.

21
00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:12.518
Describe.

22
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:16.085
Describe means to say what something is like.

23
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:18.567
Describe a place you visited.

24
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:21.638
Your turn. Say: Describe.

25
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.640
Describe.

26
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:27.094
Prompt.

27
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:30.617
Prompt means a bullet point that guides your talk.

28
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.647
Answer every prompt.

29
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:35.566
Your turn. Say: Prompt.

30
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.134
Prompt.

31
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:40.838
Anecdote.

32
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:44.244
Anecdote means a short true story.

33
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.675
Include a short anecdote.

34
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.843
Your turn. Say: Anecdote.

35
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:53.678
Anecdote.

36
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:55.371
Memorable.

37
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:58.522
Memorable means easy to remember.

38
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:00.768
It was a memorable trip.

39
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:03.734
Your turn. Say: Memorable.

40
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.636
Memorable.

41
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:09.315
Conclude.

42
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:12.804
Conclude means to finish with a final point.

43
00:02:13.417 --> 00:02:15.045
Conclude with how you felt.

44
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.919
Your turn. Say: Conclude.

45
00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:21.640
Conclude.

46
00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:26.409
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.226
Visal, how does Part 2 work?

48
00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:37.915
The examiner gives you a cue card. You have one minute to prepare and then you speak for one to two minutes without interruption.

49
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:40.610
How should I use the one minute?

50
00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:49.884
Write keywords, not sentences. Use the prompts on the card as a plan, and add a feeling or a reason for each point.

51
00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:52.948
What if I run out of ideas?

52
00:02:54.050 --> 00:03:05.865
Keep talking. Add a short anecdote or describe how you felt. The examiner only stops you at two minutes, so a steady, relaxed pace is better than a fast one.

53
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.558
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:13.727
Grammar focus: Strategy: use the prompts as your plan.

55
00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.213
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:18.717
I'd like to talk about a trip that I took last year.

57
00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:22.243
What I remember most is how peaceful it felt.

58
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:30.380
Use the one minute to note keywords. Follow the prompts in order, add details and feelings, and finish with a short conclusion.

59
00:03:31.117 --> 00:03:34.733
Be careful! Don't say: I write full sentences in my notes.

60
00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:39.270
Say: I write only keywords in my notes.

61
00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:40.896
Note keywords.

62
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.561
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.612
Describe a Trip.

64
00:03:46.912 --> 00:03:50.351
The cue card says: describe a trip you remember.

65
00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.725
Vanna notes four keywords: where, who, what, feeling.

66
00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:59.312
She talks about a boat ride on the Tonle Sap with her grandfather.

67
00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.670
She tells a short anecdote about seeing the sunset on the water.

68
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.398
She concludes that it was peaceful and unforgettable.

69
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.467
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:15.409
How long do you prepare in Part 2?

71
00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:19.548
A, no time. B, one minute. C, five minutes.

72
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.018
The answer is B: one minute.

73
00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:28.380
During preparation you should write blank.

74
00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:33.634
A, full sentences. B, an essay. C, keywords.

75
00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.501
The answer is C: keywords.

76
00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.208
The prompts are your blank.

77
00:04:42.508 --> 00:04:46.800
A, plan. B, title. C, answers to Part 3.

78
00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.030
The answer is A: plan.

79
00:04:53.183 --> 00:04:54.637
Where was Vanna's trip?

80
00:04:54.937 --> 00:04:58.892
A, Kampot. B, the Tonle Sap. C, Angkor Wat.

81
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:04.909
The answer is B: the Tonle Sap.

82
00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:07.388
How long do you speak?

83
00:05:07.688 --> 00:05:12.723
A, thirty seconds. B, five minutes. C, one to two minutes.

84
00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.777
The answer is C: one to two minutes.

85
00:05:19.967 --> 00:05:22.991
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.966
Describe a memorable trip you took.

87
00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.134
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:50.757
I'd like to talk about a boat trip on the Tonle Sap that I took with my grandfather. We went at sunset, and the water was calm and golden. I remember it clearly because it was peaceful, and it was the first time we travelled together.

89
00:05:51.057 --> 00:05:52.732
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:53.617 --> 00:05:58.939
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: use the prompts as your plan.

91
00:05:59.239 --> 00:06:03.761
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

92
00:06:04.061 --> 00:06:06.644
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.944 --> 00:06:09.271
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

